    <string name="t_008">Full access is active. All available checks will run.</string>
    <string name="t_009">A deep check can find more, such as running background processes.\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_010">Set up Shizuku once. Root is not needed.</string>
    <string name="t_011">Set up deep check</string>
    <string name="t_012">Install Shizuku. It lets Spyhound check more of your phone.</string>
    <string name="t_013">Installation failed? Download Shizuku from shizuku.rikka.app. On Samsung, Auto Blocker may\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_014">block installation. You can turn it off in Security and privacy.</string>
    <string name="t_015">Install Shizuku</string>
    <string name="t_016">Open Settings → About phone and tap Build number seven times.\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_017">Samsung: About phone → Software information → Build number.</string>
    <string name="t_018">Nothing happens? Tap faster. Android may ask for your PIN.</string>
    <string name="t_019">Open phone info</string>
    <string name="t_020">In Shizuku, tap Pairing. Allow Shizuku notifications.\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_021">In Developer options, turn on Wireless debugging. Then tap Pair device with pairing code.\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_022">Enter code in Shizuku notification. Then tap Start in Shizuku.</string>
    <string name="t_023">Pairing code rejected? Check that Shizuku notifications are allowed.\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_024">Use split screen to see Settings and notification together.\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_025">Samsung: turn off Auto Blocker. If Shizuku keeps searching for pairing service, allow it to run in background\u0020</string>
    <string name="t_026">(Battery: Unrestricted).</string>
    <string name="t_027">Open Shizuku</string>
    <string name="t_028">Open Developer options</string>
    <string name="t_029">Spyhound needs your permission to use Shizuku. Tap Allow when Android asks.</string>
    <string name="t_030">No dialog? Make sure Shizuku is running (step 3). Reopen Spyhound and try again.</string>
    <string name="t_031">Allow Spyhound</string>
    <string name="t_032">Have root? Tap Request root on the start screen.</string>
    <string name="t_033">Deep check is ready</string>
    <string name="t_034">You can turn off Wireless debugging afterward. Shizuku keeps running until next restart.</string>
